{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790361406,"nonce":"ktPRJ9jz6hhgQCDWXLppCb9O6zc=","title":"Multi-shot resumption re-enters the performer's state machine instead of copying it","message":"`__zyntax_effect_resume` (crates/zyntax_embed/src/effect_runtime.rs) writes the resumed value and the resume state into the performer's state machine and re-polls that same machine until Ready. A second `k(v)` does it again over whatever the first run left: slots the first run overwrote at later suspensions, and resources it released on its way out. A performer that makes a fiber before the perform frees it at return (`emit_fiber_drops`), so a second `k` resumes a freed fiber; crates/zynml/tests/async_effect_composition.rs records this as a limitation of sync and async handlers alike. Multi-shot is sound only when the code after the perform reads nothing but values saved before it and releases nothing.\n\nDone: either each resumption after the first runs on a copy of the continuation (the state machine cloned at the perform, with owned resources duplicated or the copy refused), or a second resumption of a continuation that owns resources is refused with a diagnostic. A test resumes twice across a performer that owns a fiber.","files":null}]}